      ],
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "The prime extensor of the medial four fingers at the metacarpophalangeal joints, acting through the extensor expansion. It crosses the wrist dorsally and clearly assists wrist extension, giving a minor contribution to holding the wrist neutral under load; as a finger extensor it is an antagonist to grip, not a grip muscle.",
      "status": "reviewed"
    },
    {
