        },
        {
          "demand": "wrist_stability",
          "weight": 0.5
        }
      ],
      "confidence": "medium",
      "rationale": "With the ulnar head, it forms the strongest wrist flexor and ulnar deviator, so the whole-muscle weight is split between the two heads. Its medial epicondyle origin gives a minor dynamic restraint against elbow valgus, and it co-contracts to hold the wrist neutral under load.",
      "status": "reviewed"
    },
