      ],
      "confidence": "medium",
      "rationale": "The larger head of flexor digitorum superficialis. It flexes the proximal interphalangeal and metacarpophalangeal joints as a major helper to flexor digitorum profundus, making it a major grip contributor, and assists wrist flexion. Its elbow flexion moment is negligible and omitted.",
      "status": "reviewed"
    },
    {
